@meta
id: 20-09
title: Drill — swap in the yank
chapter: 20
type: drill
skills: register-blackhole
par: 36
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: copy the string, then double-click and paste, twice
open: order.provider.spec.ts

@brief
Eight times: the two `'EXPIRED'` strings should be the full
`'REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED'` declared at the top. Yank the real one once,
then replace each short one without ever losing the yank.

@keys
| `yi'` | yank inside the quotes |
| `"_di'` | delete inside the quotes, into nothing |
| `P` | put the yank back inside |
| `n` | next match |

@hints
`yi'` works from anywhere on the line before the quotes. Then
`/'EXPIRED'` Enter, `"_di'`, `P`, `n`, and the same again.
--
Without `"_` the second `P` would put `EXPIRED` — the first `di'`
would have replaced the yank. That is the whole drill.

@solution
    yi'  /'EXPIRED'<Enter> "_di'P  n "_di'P  :wq<Enter>

Yank once, then `"_di'P` as one unit at every match. It is a chord
worth owning: delete-into-nothing followed by put is how you replace
text with the yank as many times as you like, and the dot command in
chapter 11 cannot do it because a put is not a change of the deleted
text.

Chapter 22 adds a second way, `vi'p`, which is shorter and has its own
clobbering trap. `"_` is the honest one.

@start order.provider.spec.ts
const reason = 'REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED';

it('records the reason outside the window', async () => {
  const result = await provider.cancel(staleOrder.id);

  expect(result.cancellationReason).toBe('EXPIRED');
  expect(reveal(orderRepository).update).toHaveBeenCalledWith({
    where: { id: staleOrder.id },
    values: { status: 'CANCELLED', cancellationReason: 'EXPIRED' },
  });
});

@expected order.provider.spec.ts
const reason = 'REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED';

it('records the reason outside the window', async () => {
  const result = await provider.cancel(staleOrder.id);

  expect(result.cancellationReason).toBe('REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED');
  expect(reveal(orderRepository).update).toHaveBeenCalledWith({
    where: { id: staleOrder.id },
    values: { status: 'CANCELLED', cancellationReason: 'REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED' },
  });
});
